```java
// Requires nums to be SORTED ascending
int binarySearch(int[] nums, int target) {
    int left = 0, right = nums.length - 1;
    while (left <= right) {
        int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;   // overflow-safe midpoint
        if (nums[mid] == target) return mid;   // found
        else if (nums[mid] < target) left = mid + 1;  // go right
        else right = mid - 1;                  // go left
    }
    return -1;   // exhausted the range
}
// 1,000,000 elements -> about 20 comparisons
```
The only cost of binary search is keeping the data sorted; the payoff is the jump from O(n) to O(log n).

